      "created_at": "2014-08-14T04:51:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The innate power that Baron Blade gets in his scenario #1 is Power Splice:</p><blockquote><p><b>Unlimited</b><span>&nbsp;If there is a scenario marker within range of 1 of your character, roll 3 dice. &nbsp;Any dice that roll a 5 or a 6 count as successes.</span></p></blockquote><p>The Scenario Powers setup says, \"Upon getting a first success on a scenario marker, flip that marker away from its initial side. &nbsp;Upon getting a second success, remove that marker.\" &nbsp;If a Power Splice roll comes up 1, 5, and 6, does that count as two successes and remove the marker? &nbsp;That's how we played in our opening game, but if I misinterpreted that I'd like to know for future play.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:08.455Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
