      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>The innate power that Baron Blade gets in his scenario #1 is Power Splice:</p><blockquote><p><b style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px; background-color: rgb(235, 233, 234);\">Unlimited</b><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px; background-color: rgb(235, 233, 234);\">&nbsp;If there is a scenario marker within range of 1 of your character, roll 3 dice. &nbsp;Any dice that roll a 5 or a 6 count as successes.</span></p></blockquote><p>The Scenario Powers setup says, &quot;Upon getting a first success on a scenario marker, flip that marker away from its initial side. &nbsp;Upon getting a second success, remove that marker.&quot; &nbsp;If a Power Splice roll comes up 1, 5, and 6, does that count as two successes and remove the marker? &nbsp;That&#39;s how we played in our opening game, but if I misinterpreted that I&#39;d like to know for future play.</p>",
